  "description": "ρ_K LO piece: numerical verification of the [Wenzl 1988] Markov-multiplicativity / branching identity χ^λ(β_p ⊗ β_n) = Σ c^λ_{μν} χ^μ(β_p) χ^ν(β_n) for the deuteron decomposition H_6 ↓ H_3 × H_3 at q_0, across all λ ⊢ 6.  Max relative deviation 3.02e-70 at _precision.COMPUTE_DPS (70) — quote this witness's own max_relative_deviation, not a figure from prose.  This read 'machine precision (~1e-14)' until 2026-09-14, and that number was a property of the ARITHMETIC, not of the identity: the probe took char_fast's double-precision path, whose sigma matrices are dtype=complex and whose products are numpy, so complex128 was the floor no matter how precise q_0 was.  Re-run on the mpmath path the residue falls 56 orders, which strengthens rather than changes the conclusion — the LO piece of prop:rho-k-graded-expansion is a theorem (Markov multiplicativity + free-constituent additivity), not an empirical ansatz.  NOTE for a reader comparing artifacts: rho-k-graded-expansion.md still cites 3.2e-14 as the verification figure, i.e. UNDERSTATES this probe by 56 orders; that block belongs to the mass-endomorphism arc and was deliberately not edited here.  Also confirms trace-level multiplicativity tr_M(β_p ⊗ β_n) = tr_M(β_p)·tr_M(β_n).",
